[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T10:20:21-08:00","id":1498319,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>Witchypoo</u></i></b><br /> A Goblin Queen, not much is known of <b>Witchypoo</b>, other than that she is <b>not originally a hob</b>, having acquired enough Goblin Debt to be transformed into her current state. Possessing strange bodily mutations doubling as powers, Witchypoo can consult ghosts <i>and</i> Hedge ghosts alike in pursuit of occult truths.<br /> <br /> Witchypoo lives in the Hedge town of Bucketown, where she runs the only business there <i>not</i> centered around death: a candy store.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-30-2022, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T12:15:15-08:00","id":1498329,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>The Dylan family</u></i></b><br /> Consisting entirely of mortals (as far as the freehold can tell), the <b>Dylan family</b> is <i>the</i> most important dynasty in Lambry County. It runs <b>Dylan Ranch</b>, which, despite the singular name, is actually a <i>series</i> of farms, ranches and cattle ranges owned by the Dylans as a whole.<br /> <br /> <b>The Trapper Estate</b>, where <b>Candlelit Circle</b> meets twice a week\u2014-once on Saturday, staying the night at the place til Sunday night. They have a strict policy of no solicitors, rumors fly thick as thieves as on what exactly goes on at these meetings.<br /> <br /> The family patriarch is <b>Casper Dylan</b>, a multi-millionaire self-made businessman, now in his 80s. Casper belongs to <b>Candlelit Circle</b>.<br /> <br /> The family matriarch is <b>Marissa Dylan</b>, paralyzed below the neck many <i>many</i> years ago ago in a car accident. No one\u2019s seen the woman in decades.<br /> <br /> The chief judge in Lambry County, <b>Prudence Dylan</b>, is the middle-aged daughter of Casper and Marissa. She\u2019s known for her vindictive streak. She belongs to <b>Candlelit Circle</b>.<br /> <br /> More to come.<br /> <br /> New mystery cult:<br /> <b>Candlelit Circle</b> (<i>Mystery Cult Initiation * through *****</i>)<br /> <b>Candlelit Circle</b> is a not-so-Secret Society all the mortal movers and shakers in Lambry County, Montana, belong to. Billing itself a split-off from the Freemasons, Candlelit Circle is <i>very</i> secretive about its own affairs.<br /> * To be filled in much later on.<br /> ** To be filled in much later on.<br /> *** To be filled in much later on.<br /> **** To be filled in much later on.<br /> ***** To be filled in much later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-30-2022, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T08:15:41-08:00","id":1498441,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>The Estates</u></i></b><br /> Also referred to as \u2018the boonies\u2019, <b>the Estates</b> are \u2018fringe\u2019 people\u2019 living in out-of-the-way places throughout Lambry County, Montana. They are a population, rather than a location. People dwelling in the Estates is a social statement, too, and the message is clear: <i>Fuck off</i>!<br /> <br /> Most of the inhabitants of the Estates are mundane people: survivalists, eccentrics and reclusive paranoiacs, but, every now and again, someone supernatural will pop up, such as <b>Daniel Oberloch</b> (thought by the freehold to be a witch) or <b>Mr. Coates</b> (a crazy survivalist some in the freehold say has a demon inside him).<br /> <br /> Strange things happen in the Estates, and the reclusiveness of its inhabitants means very little of this strangeness gets reported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T11:07:30-08:00","id":1499080,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>The Juniper Crew</u></i></b><br /> Hired by the Dylan patriarch, <b>the Juniper Crew</b> are nearly twenty men and women hired to keep <b>Juniper Lake</b> as clean as possible. During the spring and summer, they act as informal lifeguards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}